# Everything at this level is ignored by default, and only the application is
# tracked. This is a deliberate allow-list, not an ignore-list: the same directory
# holds firmware images, Ghidra projects, packet captures and a JDK, and any
# future folder added here must be allowed on purpose rather than remembered by
# whoever writes the next rule.
/*
!/.gitignore
!/NightStalkerCompanion/
!/notes/

# Inside notes/ the same rule applies one level down. The protocol documentation
# is tracked; the working notes are not. Half of that directory is session scratch
# that quotes a device UDID and a home directory, so `git add notes/` must not be
# able to pick them up: a note joins the repository by being named here.
/notes/*
!/notes/PROTOCOL.md
!/notes/CMD_TABLE.md
!/notes/FIRMWARE.md
!/notes/APP_FIELDS.md
!/notes/CONNECTIVITY.md
!/notes/RE_FINDINGS.md
!/notes/MAUI_PORT.md
!/notes/DEVICE_DEPLOY.md
!/notes/WINDOW_RUNBOOK.md
# HANDOFF.md is session notes by nature, but five code comments cite it as the
# source of the read-back lag and of what is still uncaptured; a comment that
# points at an ignored file is a dead link. It stays until those citations move
# into the durable documents.
!/notes/HANDOFF.md

# Build output and IDE state
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.userprefs

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Test and coverage output
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
*.coverage
*.coveragexml
coverage*.json
coverage*.xml
